The AMDGPU plugin is ordinary HSA host code and its sources already carry
non-x86 fallbacks (offload/plugins-nextgen/amdgpu/src/rtl.cpp guards the
synchronous-copy paths with __i386__/__x86_64__), but the plugin gate in
offload/CMakeLists.txt only whitelists x86_64/ppc64le/aarch64 hosts.  On
loongarch64 the requested plugin was therefore removed from
LIBOMPTARGET_PLUGINS_TO_BUILD, leaving that list empty, and the unquoted
string(STRIP) on the next lines failed with:
  CMake Error at offload/CMakeLists.txt:214 (string):
    string sub-command STRIP requires two arguments.

--- a/offload/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/offload/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -187,7 +187,7 @@
   message(STATUS "Not building host plugin: only Linux systems are supported")
   list(REMOVE_ITEM LIBOMPTARGET_PLUGINS_TO_BUILD "host")
 endif()
-if(NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "(x86_64)|(ppc64le)|(aarch64)$"
+if(NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR MATCHES "(x86_64)|(ppc64le)|(aarch64)|(loongarch64)$"
         AND CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux"))
   if("amdgpu" IN_LIST LIBOMPTARGET_PLUGINS_TO_BUILD)
     message(STATUS "Not building AMDGPU plugin: only support AMDGPU in "
